---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

// PLACEHOLDER. Written to describe what the waitlist page actually does, so
// it is accurate today, but it is not legal advice and has not been reviewed.
// Replace before launch.
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How Frym handles the information you give us when you join the waitlist."
	updated="14 August 2026"
>
	<p>
		This page explains what Frym collects while it is in pre-launch, and what we
		do with it. Frym is not yet available, and this site does not offer a
		product or an account.
	</p>

	<section>
		<h2>What we collect</h2>
		<p>
			If you join the waitlist, we store the email address you give us and, if
			you provide one, your first name. If you answer the optional question
			after signing up, we store your answer alongside your email address.
		</p>
		<p>
			We do not run advertising trackers on this site, and we do not sell or
			share what you give us.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Why we collect it</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>To tell you when early access opens.</li>
			<li>To send occasional updates about how Frym is coming along.</li>
			<li>
				To understand which problems people most want solved, so we build the
				right first version.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
		<p>
			Until Frym launches and you have had the chance to take up early access,
			or until you ask us to remove it — whichever comes first.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Your choices</h2>
		<p>
			You can ask us to send you a copy of what we hold, correct it, or delete
			it. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>{' '}
			and we will action it.
		</p>
		<p>
			Every update we send includes an unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing removes
			you from the waitlist.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>
			If this policy changes in a way that affects people already on the
			waitlist, we will say so in an email rather than only updating this page.
		</p>
	</section>
</LegalLayout>
